  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responsible Business Conduct in Latin America and the Caribbean (ILO and OHCHR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsible Business Conduct in Latin America and the Caribbean (RBCLAC) i&lt;/strong&gt;mplemented by OECD/ILO/UNOHCHR. It targets nine countries (AR, BR, CL, CO, CR, EC, ME, PA, PE). The Project aims to promote smart, sustainable and inclusive economic growth in the region by supporting responsible business conduct (RBC) practices in line with international instruments. The programme contains three main components:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;- &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Component 1. Supporting business capacity to conduct due diligence in priority sectors&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Component 2. Strengthening the role of governments in promoting RBC&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Component 3. Fostering workers&#xbf; organisations and other stakeholder engagement for RBC&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;Over the past years, the EU has strengthened RBC as a cornerstone of a rules-based trading system that breeds trust and resilience. RBC standards are playing a predominant role in recent EU regulatory efforts to promote responsible supply chains, as well as means to promote sustainable development through its trade and investment agreements. This unique institutional partnership on RBC in LAC sends a clear signal to governments, business, civil society and other stakeholders on coherence and alignment on international RBC expectations, and can contribute to effective implementation by business in the region.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;Under INTPA the project will increase the emphasis on supporting LAC stakeholders considering the EU&#xbf;s proposal for a directive on corporate sustainability due diligence and deforestation free products. Specific sectoral focus will be on mining and agriculture (including forestry).&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
